  "rootPlanAssessment": {
    "fallbackTranslationsNeeded": false,
    "falsyUsername": "Without the proposed trigger guard, a falsy username makes fetchInterests return before setting interestsLoading and leaves the !interests branch reachable, so null would make an empty popup. With username && <Popup>, that popup is not mounted and there is no empty popup for a falsy username.",
    "nullFallback": "Accept with a transition caveat: with a truthy username, the active-loading branch renders the new status, the error branch renders its error, and successful fetch stores an object (including an empty object). The !interests fallback has no settled visible state. Returning null is safe once the popup is guarded for falsy username.",
    "popupGuard": "Accept: rendering the interests Popup only when username is truthy prevents opening the interests popup without an identity. It complements the early return already in fetchInterests.",
    "recommendation": "Apply the username guard; move the new localized sentence into the interestsLoading branch alongside the spinner; return null from the later !interests branch. Retain a neutral fallback only if the runtime shows a visible blank transition.",
    "transitionRisk": "Popup content is initially null while interests is null and loading is false. A blank first frame is possible if the Popup commits its open state before the onOpen parent state update; React event batching is likely to combine these updates, but this static review cannot guarantee rendering order. There is no persistent empty state with the guard and loading transition."
  },
